---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';
const site = siteFromHost();
const path = "/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-activecampaign";
const title = "Yotpo Email & SMS to ActiveCampaign: Shopify migration decisions";
const desc = "Yotpo messaging has been decommissioned. Evaluate ActiveCampaign as a replacement for store messaging and sales workflows while deciding separately whether to retain Yotpo Reviews and Loyalty.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I keep Yotpo Reviews while changing email platforms?",
    "answer": "Treat Reviews as a separate active product decision. Document the sender for review requests and the supported route for any data needed in ActiveCampaign; do not assume that the retired messaging product remains part of the stack."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I export my old Yotpo messaging account now?",
    "answer": "Do not plan on dashboard access. The decommission notice says it is inactive. Start with records already available and establish any recovery options with support before committing to a migration date."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
    <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a></nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p></header>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>This is a replacement decision</h2>
      <p>Yotpo announced full Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025. Its current lifecycle notice says the application is decommissioned and dashboard access and background services are inactive. A new Yotpo messaging trial, bundle renewal or parallel Yotpo send test is therefore not an available buying premise. Reviews and Loyalty are separate decisions; their usefulness does not restore the retired sender.</p>
      <h2>Reconstruct the data you can actually obtain</h2>
      <p>Begin with Shopify customer and order records, prior exports you already hold and documented consent or suppression records. Do not assume the retired Yotpo dashboard can still export contacts, history or templates. If records are missing, establish what support can recover before scheduling a launch. Missing permission history is not permission to treat every old phone number or email address as subscribed.</p>
      <h2>Shopify history has plan implications</h2>
      <p>ActiveCampaign documents using Shopify data for follow-up email, automation and segments. Its integration guide says historical sync is unavailable on Starter. Distinguish historical order import from new events in your plan selection: a winback segment based on prior purchases cannot be validated using only newly created test orders. Inspect order status and customer matching as well as the presence of a contact.</p>
      <h2>Wholesale follow-up is a separate workflow</h2>
      <p>For a hypothetical store selling to both consumers and trade buyers, define the field that identifies a wholesale inquiry and the staff member who owns follow-up. Rehearse routing that inquiry while excluding it from the consumer discount welcome. ActiveCampaign lists CRM and SMS capabilities, but do not assume every plan includes the sales features, seats or channel coverage you need. Request a configuration that includes the actual workflow, rather than buying on a generic CRM label.</p>
      <h2>Retain Reviews or Loyalty only with clear ownership</h2>
      <p>Keeping a review widget or a points program does not require retaining retired Yotpo messaging. Inventory which active application sends review requests, rewards notices and promotional email. For any proposed transfer of review or points data into ActiveCampaign, establish the supported connector or field mapping first; this page does not promise a native integration. Missing loyalty data should omit the personalization rather than display a fabricated balance.</p>
      <h2>Budget the replacement rather than an obsolete bundle</h2>
      <p>Use ActiveCampaign’s current pricing for the required contact size, automation plan and any sales or messaging additions. Include retained Yotpo modules and integration maintenance separately. Rebuild a disabled welcome and recovery flow, inspect consent and purchase exits, then activate one owner per trigger. ActiveCampaign belongs on the shortlist when store email and sales follow-up need shared automation; a simple DTC newsletter does not by itself justify adding a sales pipeline.</p>
      <h2>Primary sources</h2>
      <p>Product information checked November 25, 2026. <a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">Yotpo retirement</a> · <a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Live lifecycle notice</a> · <a class="link" href="https://help.activecampaign.com/hc/en-us/articles/115000202150-Connect-your-Shopify-store-to-ActiveCampaign">ActiveCampaign Shopify integration</a> · <a class="link" href="https://www.activecampaign.com/pricing">ActiveCampaign plans</a></p>
    </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/drip-vs-activecampaign">Drip vs ActiveCampaign</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/privy-vs-activecampaign">Privy vs ActiveCampaign</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-drip">Yotpo vs Drip</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/b2b-wholesale">Email apps for B2B wholesale</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/beauty">Email apps for beauty stores</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Questions about this comparison" />
</BaseLayout>
